---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

/**
 * Dit beleid moet beschrijven wat de site fetitelijk doet, niet wat we van plan
 * zijn. Verandert er iets aan de verwerking — analytics, advertenties — dan gaat
 * deze pagina eerst om, en pas daarna de code.
 */
const updated = '30 August 2026';

const title = 'Privacy — HumanAverage';
const description =
  'What HumanAverage does and does not collect. No accounts, no analytics, no advertising ' +
  'code, and your measurements never leave your browser.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description} canonical="/privacy/">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>What we collect: almost nothing</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Your height and weight are never sent to us. The percentile is calculated inside your
        own browser, from a data file your browser already downloaded.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow content">
      <p class="field-hint">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <h2>The values you enter</h2>
      <p>
        When you enter your age, sex and a measurement, those values stay in the memory of the
        page you have open. They are used to look up a position in a table that was downloaded
        with the page, and they disappear when you reload or close it. Nothing is transmitted to
        us, and no account is created.
      </p>

      <h3>What your browser remembers</h3>
      <p>
        On the European comparison pages there is one exception. The country and the age you enter
        are saved in this browser's local storage, under a single key, so that the next page
        already knows them instead of asking again. That storage sits on your own device: it is
        never sent to us, there is no server behind it, and no profile of you exists anywhere
        else. Clearing site data for this domain removes it, and a private window keeps nothing at
        all.
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>One exception you control.</strong> If you press “copy link to this result”,
          the link that is created contains your age, sex and measurement as part of the web
          address — that is what makes the result shareable. It is placed on your clipboard and
          goes nowhere else. But anyone you send that link to can read those values from it, so
          share it deliberately.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no cookies, runs no analytics, and contains no advertising code. There is
        nothing to consent to, so we do not ask.
      </p>
      <p>
        That may change. If analytics or advertising is ever added, this page will be updated
        before the code goes live, and where consent is legally required it will be requested
        through an appropriate consent platform — with no non-essential cookies set before you
        have chosen.
      </p>

      <h2>Technically necessary data</h2>
      <p>
        As with virtually any website, the hosting provider processes technical request data:
        an IP address, the time, the page requested, browser information and errors. This is
        necessary to deliver the site securely. HumanAverage is hosted by
        <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener">Vercel</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do also use Google Search Console, which reports how the site performs in Google
        Search. It shows aggregated figures — how often pages appeared and were clicked — and
        does not identify individual visitors to us.
      </p>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        We link to the CDC, to scientific publishers and to source datasets. Once you open one
        of those, that party's own privacy policy applies. We never pass your entered values
        along in such a link.
      </p>

      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        If you email <a href="mailto:firenature23@gmail.com">firenature23@gmail.com</a> we
        receive your address, your message and anything else you choose to include, and use it
        only to handle your question. Email is processed through Gmail, so Google's privacy
        policy also applies. Please do not send passwords, medical records or other sensitive
        information.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Because we never receive your measurements, we cannot show you, correct or delete them —
        there is nothing on our side to act on. For questions about other data, about deleting
        an email you sent us, or about this policy, write to
        <a href="mailto:firenature23@gmail.com">firenature23@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .field-hint { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  </style>
</Base>
